(text "Correct input polarity"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 73.7200 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00418694-84d9-40ed-b6ba-ebaa69861f43")
	)

(text "DC input\nJ30001 connects the external 24 V supply\nto +24V_RAW and GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.5200 123.1900 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0a5f1d17-8b4e-4c09-a0ae-fe9d02dbe524")
	)

(text "J30001 is the external DC input connector. Pin 1 connects to +24V_RAW; pin 2\nconnects to GND, the input return. The +24V_RAW net supplies the downstream\ninput-protection circuitry. R30001, D30002 and D30001 form a polarity\nindicator connected across the input terminals."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.8600 59.4160 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "35757349-ec04-4262-b3cb-44a22bb860ba")
	)

(text "Polarity indication\nD30001 (green): correct input polarity.\nD30002 (red): reversed input polarity."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86.3600 88.9000 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b79853b-c6c4-4a00-aeac-03036a9a0162")
	)

(text "NAME: Input Connector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.3200 33.0200 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 86 96 108 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "71ed51b3-2805-416e-a66d-6dfa273b2551")
	)

(text "Green indicates correct input polarity; red indicates reversed input polarity.\nBoth LEDs are off when no input voltage is present.\n\nThis circuit indicates polarity but does not prevent reverse voltage from\nreaching downstream components. Reverse-polarity protection is provided by a\nseparate protection stage. The green LED does not confirm that a fuse is\nintact, that an eFuse is enabled, or that downstream power rails are\noperating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 151.0700 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7ae9651f-9d9e-4d83-823b-1646dac7ff6b")
	)

(text "24 V Input Connector and Polarity Indicator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.8600 40.2100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.6 2.6)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 25 47 72 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b7e68de-09ed-4e93-ad60-6618bed83b61")
	)

(text "Meaning of the indication"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 146.0500 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90f8a053-83a0-457a-9c86-221024f460ba")
	)

(text "R30001 is 10 kOhm. At an input magnitude of 24 V and an assumed LED forward\nvoltage of 2.0 V, the current is approximately 2.2 mA. R30001 dissipates\napproximately 48 mW. Actual current depends on the forward voltage of the\nconducting LED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 130.8100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ee7c325-6685-4a8d-9f71-ddfb5d3e70b3")
	)

(text "Reversed input polarity"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 99.1200 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "acd4f087-a20b-4439-860d-d91895e22ab7")
	)

(text "If the supply leads are reversed, +24V_RAW becomes negative relative to GND.\nCurrent flows from GND through the red LED D30002 and R30001 to J30001 pin 1.\nD30002 illuminates, indicating reversed input polarity; D30001 remains off.\n\nIn this condition, D30002 limits the reverse voltage across D30001. R30001\nlimits the indicator current in either direction."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 104.1400 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cd2055a4-a646-4372-8ca3-4000964d7c44")
	)

(text "When J30001 pin 1 is positive relative to pin 2, current flows from +24V_RAW\nthrough R30001 and the green LED D30001 to GND. D30001 illuminates, indicating\ncorrect input polarity. The red LED D30002 is reverse-biased and remains off.\n\nThe LEDs are connected in antiparallel, so D30001 limits the reverse voltage\nacross D30002 approximately to its own forward voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.9400 78.7400 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d16f32b3-46a6-4069-ad26-3a7375088132")
	)

(text "Purpose and connections"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.8600 54.3960 0)
